+// Frametop: sends one Opus packet of the client's microphone (mono, 48 kHz) to the host on the
+// encrypted control stream: packet type 0x3003 (Apollo protocol extension range), its payload a
+// 4-byte header [sequence high, sequence low, channels (1), flags (0)] and the Opus packet, the
+// layout of Vibepollo PR #169. Reliable, on a channel of its own: ENet's throttle drops unreliable
+// packets whenever round trips wobble, a quarter of them on Wi-Fi beside video. Hosts without
+// Frametop's build ignore it. Returns 0 when sent, -1 when the control stream isn't connected or
+// isn't encrypted (never sent in the clear), -2 for an Opus packet over
+// LI_MICROPHONE_MAX_OPUS_BYTES, -3 when ENet couldn't send it.
+#define LI_MICROPHONE_MAX_OPUS_BYTES 240
+int LiSendMicrophoneOpusData(const unsigned char* opusData, int opusLength);
